# node_exporter.service — Host-first deployment systemd unit

## Overview

This systemd unit runs **node_exporter 1.12.1** for the LLM proxy stack
monitoring infrastructure. It uses the host-first model (binary in
`~/bin/node_exporter/`, no containers) and is deployed as a **systemd user
service** with `loginctl enable-linger`.

node_exporter is the **only** exporter this stack runs. It provides:

- the standard host metrics (CPU, load, memory, filesystem, network, systemd
  state) that explain proxy and llama-server behaviour under load; and
- the GPU signal, via two collectors:

  | Collector | Series | Source |
  |---|---|---|
  | `--collector.hwmon` | `node_hwmon_power_average_watt`, `node_hwmon_chip_names`, `node_hwmon_temp_celsius`, … | `/sys/class/hwmon` — the `amdgpu` chip's `power1` sensor is GPU package power |
  | `--collector.textfile.directory` | `gpu_gtt_used_bytes`, `gpu_vram_used_bytes`, `gpu_vram_total_bytes`, `gpu_busy_percent` | `*.prom` files written by the 10 s sysfs sampler in [gpu-metrics.service](gpu-metrics.service) |

node_exporter has **no amdgpu collector**, which is why GPU memory comes
through the textfile collector rather than being read directly. The
AMD-authored exporter that would have provided those series
(`amd/rocm-exporter`) publishes no release artefacts — see
[rocm-exporter.service](rocm-exporter.service).

### Listen address

The unit binds `127.0.0.1:9100` — **loopback only**. Prometheus scrapes it from
the same host, so there is no reason to publish it to the tailnet or the LAN,
and node_exporter has no authentication.

## User Service (recommended)

**File location**: `~/.config/systemd/user/node_exporter.service`

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Prometheus node_exporter (host + GPU sysfs metrics)
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/home/rgardler/bin/node_exporter/node_exporter \
  --web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9100 \
  --collector.textfile.directory=/home/rgardler/.local/share/node_exporter/textfile \
  --collector.hwmon
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
StandardOutput=append:/home/rgardler/.local/state/node_exporter/logs/node_exporter.log
StandardError=append:/home/rgardler/.local/state/node_exporter/logs/node_exporter.log
MemoryMax=1G

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
```

## Setup commands (user service)

```bash
# 1. Download and install the binary
NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION="1.12.1"
ARCH="linux-amd64"
wget "https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}/node_exporter-${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}.${ARCH}.tar.gz"
tar xzf "node_exporter-${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}.${ARCH}.tar.gz"
mkdir -p ~/bin/node_exporter
cp "node_exporter-${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}.${ARCH}/node_exporter" ~/bin/node_exporter/
rm -rf "node_exporter-${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}.${ARCH}" \
       "node_exporter-${NODE_EXPORTER_VERSION}.${ARCH}.tar.gz"

# 2. Create the textfile collector directory and the log directory.
#    The textfile directory must match --collector.textfile.directory above;
#    gpu-metrics.service writes gpu.prom into it.
mkdir -p ~/.local/share/node_exporter/textfile
mkdir -p ~/.local/state/node_exporter/logs

# 3. Install the unit. docs/systemd/*.service are documents that wrap the unit
#    in an `ini` block, so the block is extracted — `cp` would install markdown.
mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
awk '/^```ini$/{f=1;next} /^```$/{f=0} f' \
  docs/systemd/node_exporter.service \
  > ~/.config/systemd/user/node_exporter.service

# 4. Enable and start
systemctl --user daemon-reload
systemctl --user enable --now node_exporter.service

# 5. Verify
systemctl --user status node_exporter.service
journalctl --user -u node_exporter.service -n 20
```

The sampler ([gpu-metrics.service](gpu-metrics.service)) can be installed
before or after this unit; node_exporter picks up `gpu.prom` on the next
scrape as soon as the file exists.

## Metric names

GPU series (from the textfile collector — see gpu-metrics.service for how each
value is sampled and refreshed every 10 s):

| Series | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `gpu_gtt_used_bytes` | gauge | GTT (system RAM mapped for the GPU) in use — **the meaningful memory pool on this APU** |
| `gpu_vram_used_bytes` | gauge | Used portion of the small BIOS VRAM carve-out (1 GiB here) |
| `gpu_vram_total_bytes` | gauge | Size of the VRAM carve-out |
| `gpu_busy_percent` | gauge | Driver-reported busy percentage. **Pinned at 100% on this APU regardless of GPU state — not a utilisation signal**; scraped for continuity only |

GPU power (from the hwmon collector):

| Series | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `node_hwmon_power_average_watt{chip_name="amdgpu",sensor="power1"}` | GPU package power in watts — the utilisation signal (idle ≈ 40-54 W, computing ≈ 115 W) |
| `node_hwmon_chip_names{chip_name="amdgpu"}` | Join key that selects the amdgpu chip by name instead of a host-specific chip id |

Host series used by the cookbook and alerts:
`node_load1`, `node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes`, `node_filesystem_avail_bytes`,
`node_network_receive_bytes_total`, `node_cpu_seconds_total`,
`node_systemd_unit_state`.

## Verification

```bash
# The exporter is listening on loopback only
ss -tln | grep ':9100'
# expected: 127.0.0.1:9100

# Host metrics are served
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics | grep -c '^node_'
# expected: a four-digit count (1520 on this host)

# GPU power is visible through the hwmon collector
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics | grep 'node_hwmon_power_average_watt' | grep amdgpu
# expected: one line per amdgpu power sensor, e.g.
#   node_hwmon_power_average_watt{chip="0000:00:08_1_0000:c5:00_0",chip_name="amdgpu",sensor="power1"} 49.076

# GPU memory is visible through the textfile collector (needs gpu-metrics.service)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics | grep -E '^gpu_(gtt_used|vram_used|vram_total|busy_percent)'
# expected: four series, all with gpu="card0"

# Prometheus sees the exporter as up
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/query?query=up \
  | jq -r '.data.result[] | "\(.metric.job) \(.value[1])"'
# expected: llama-proxy 1 and node-exporter 1
```

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause / fix |
|---|---|
| Prometheus target `node-exporter` is DOWN | `systemctl --user status node_exporter.service`; check the log at `~/.local/state/node_exporter/logs/node_exporter.log` |
| `node_hwmon_*` series missing | The `amdgpu` module/binary driver is not loaded, or the running unit lacks `--collector.hwmon` — check `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics \| grep node_hwmon` and `systemctl --user cat node_exporter.service` |
| `gpu_*` series missing | `gpu-metrics.service` is not running or writes to a different directory than `--collector.textfile.directory` — see [gpu-metrics.service](gpu-metrics.service) |
| Series go stale, then vanish | node_exporter reports the textfile's mtime; Prometheus marks the target stale when scrape data stops. `systemctl --user status gpu-metrics.service` |

